          "blocks": {
            "row_1": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What's the difference between Nasal Strips and Mouth Tape?",
                "open_by_default": false
              },
              "blocks": {
                "answer": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Strips are designed to gently open the nasal passages. Tape is designed to encourage nasal breathing instead of mouth breathing while you sleep. Many people use both together.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "#000000"
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "answer"
              ]
            },
            "row_2": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What's the difference between the bundles?",
                "open_by_default": false
              },
              "blocks": {
                "answer": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Sleep Bundle comes in three colors — Breathe (Blue), Bold (Red), and Night (Black) — same two products, Strips and Tape, same price either way. The Colour Set includes all three colors of Strips, without Tape. The Season Bundle is a 3-month supply of Black Strips and Black Tape.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "#000000"
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "answer"
              ]
            },
            "row_3": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Can I buy Strips or Tape on their own?",
                "open_by_default": false
              },
              "blocks": {
                "answer": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes — both are available individually if you'd rather start with one.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "#000000"
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "answer"
              ]
            },
            "row_4": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is Mouth Tape safe to use?",
                "open_by_default": false
              },
              "blocks": {
                "answer": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Most people adjust within a few nights. If you have a cold, congestion, or any breathing condition, check with a doctor before use.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "#000000"
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "answer"
